// Live-data subscription multiplex — ONE Connect server-stream per webview for
// all live data, plus a unary control plane. Replaces the per-`<data live>` and
// per-`<Op>Live` server-stream pattern that exhausted the browser's ~6/origin
// HTTP/1.1 connection budget (measured: shell home held 12 concurrent sockets).
//
// A window opens `Open` once (mints win.<ulid> + session), opens ONE `Stream`,
// and adds/removes logical reads via unary `Subscribe`/`Unsubscribe`. The daemon
// keys a per-window subscription table on window_id and demuxes the single
// stream by subscription_id. Hand-authored (streaming isn't registry-projected).
// See docs/ship-adrs/0001-live-data-subscription-multiplex.md.

